From: XI14 <https://github.com/DavidFB-creator/MimOS>
Subject: [PATCH] users: stack the password fields so they fit at 200%

This patch was written once before, composed into exact image f5218e9e..., and
reverted. It is restored here unchanged, because the reason it was rejected is
removed by 0005 and nothing else about it was wrong.

The arithmetic, which held up: the password row lives in the right-hand pane,
not in the window, and the sidebar takes roughly 380px of the 1024px capture.
Two 200px-minimum fields plus a 24px status icon come to 424dip -- 848px at 200%
-- inside a pane of about 627px. They cannot sit side by side at any scale above
150%, with or without the validation message beside them. So they stack:

  row 1  textBoxUserPassword                          200dip -> 400px at 200%
  row 2  textBoxUserVerifiedPassword + status icon    224dip -> 448px at 200%

The rejection, which was also correct: at 200% the stacked fields clipped into
each other and the message was painted over the confirm field. The horizontal
overflow had been traded for a vertical one, because at that scale the page
overruns the pane in both axes and this patch adds a row. At 150% it was exactly
right, but 150% was already clean, so it bought nothing and cost something.

What changed is 0005. The page now lives in a scroll area, so a page taller than
the viewport scrolls instead of clipping. The added row is no longer a cost. The
two patches only make sense together: 0005 alone leaves the row overflowing
horizontally and gives it a horizontal scrollbar, which is a poor way to fill in
a form; 0006 alone is the change that was already measured and rejected.

They are kept separate on purpose. If the next exact image shows the stacking is
still wrong, 0006 can be dropped without giving up the scroll area, and the
scroll area alone still guarantees that nothing is drawn outside the pane or on
top of another widget.

The root password row gets the same treatment. MimOS hides those fields, so the
defect is not reachable there, but they are the same widgets with the same
arithmetic, and leaving one of two identical rows fixed is how a defect returns.

Only the .ui changes. UsersPage.cpp touches labelUserPassword and
labelUserPasswordError as widgets and never the layout, and nothing reparents or
re-adds them at runtime, so restructuring is confined to what uic generates.

Worth restating: the node-tree audit reported zero nameless nodes at 100%, 150%
and 200% while this page was visibly broken, before 0003, after 0003, and after
the first attempt at this patch. A count cannot see a layout. Every finding here
came from a screenshot.

Reported upstream by MimOS (XI14). See ADR-059, ADR-062 and ADR-067 in that
project.
